    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0264" n="188" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg188"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.77/1552</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-08-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 10, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Acting Minister for Foreign Affairs has informed me that the Russian Minister
                    called upon him day before yesterday and inquired <pb facs="0265" n="189"
                        xml:id="pg189"/> about reported American railway concession, stating that
                    any thereof located outside of the Great Wall would contravene a letter given by
                    the Chinese Government to the effect that Russia was to have the first option on
                    such lines. Minister for Foreign Affairs stated that he knew of no such letter
                    except the one relating to railways north and northeast of Peking, but that he
                    would look up the matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
